{"images":["data:image/webp;base64,"],"messages":[{"content":"<image> Suppose the government decided that, since gasoline is a necessity, its price should be legally capped at $1.30 per gallon. What do you anticipate would be the outcome in the gasoline market?\n\n(A) A price below that of 1.30 dollars would cause a situation of excess demand and hence a surplus.\n(B) A price below that of 1.30 dollars would cause a situation of excess demand and hence a shortage.\n(C) Not certain.\n\nAnswer with the option's letter from the given choices directly.","role":"user"}]}